Article 11
(1) Regional Government, NGOs/Social Organizations, community and family are obligated to provide protection for children from the womb in accordance with applicable Laws and Regulations.
(2) Regional Government is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence and protection of victims of violence.
(3) Prevention of the occurrence of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) in the form of:
a. conducting education on anti-violence values;
b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of prevention and protection of victims of violence.
c. forming work networks in efforts to prevent violence;
d. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
e. forming a violence prevention system; and
f. providing critical education regarding children's rights for the community.

Article 2
(1) The Regional Government is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence and protect victims of violence.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. collecting data and information about women and children as well as related laws and regulations;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values; and
c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of prevention and protection of victims of violence.
(3) Protection of victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving community elements;
b. facilitating assistance, legal aid and legal services according to the needs of victims;
c. providing housing both safe houses and alternative housing along with handling mechanisms, services, psychosocial and spiritual;
d. conducting continuous handling up to the rehabilitation and social reintegration stage;
e. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of victims of violence; and
f. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims of violence.
(4) In order to implement the responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a Regional Action Plan for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.
(5) The Regional Action Plan for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be established for a period of 3 (three) years by Decree of the Mayor.

Article 41
(1) The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out by the Women and Children Protection Service Center as an integrated Service Center to provide protection, handling and fulfillment of the rights of victims of violence.
(2) The Service Center as referred to in paragraph (1) is an implementing unit under the coordination of the Agency and is an integrated technical service unit that functions as an information center for women and children, a service center for women and children victims of violence and an empowerment center for women and children.
(3) The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. providing fast and free services to victims;
b. organizing complaint services, consultation, mediation, outreach, health, social rehabilitation, spiritual guidance, assistance, enforcement and legal aid, repatriation, social reintegration;
c. cooperating with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims;
d. networking with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperating with witness and victim protection institutions, social protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for the health recovery of victims;
e. providing convenience, comfort and safety for victims;
f. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; and
g. providing fulfillment of legal aid for victims.
(4) The institutional structure of the Women and Children Protection Service Center can be upgraded to a structural institution in the form of a Technical Implementation Unit of the Agency (UPTD) as long as it meets the criteria and requirements for the establishment of a Technical Implementation Unit of the Agency according to the provisions of the Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, institutional structure, procedures and mechanisms for organizing the Women and Children Victims of Violence Protection Service Center are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Pasal 21
Regional Governments are obligated to implement prevention of violence against children which includes:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

Article 25
Neglect as referred to in Article 21 letter d is caused by: a. actions that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. actions of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for their care;
c. actions of neglecting a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. actions that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

Article 6
(1) The provision and facilitation of protection services for women as referred to in Article 5 letter a shall be in the form of:
a. victim identification;
b. legal assistance;
c. medical rehabilitation;
d. psychosocial rehabilitation;
e. social reintegration; and
f. repatriation assistance;
(2) The provision and facilitation of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided to women:
a. victims of violence;
b. victims of human trafficking;
c. elderly who are not independent;
d. with disabilities;
e. victims of sexual exploitation;
f. heads of households;
g. in conflict-prone and disaster areas;
h. workers; and
i. other vulnerable groups.
